course: dictionary
lesson: 5908
title: Marine: the sea and beyond
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Marine means to do with the sea, or with the animals and plants that live in it. Read the words around it and the meaning is clear. «Polar bears are classed as marine mammals» tells you these bears belong to the group of mammals that live in and around the sea.
explain: «The marine iguana is the only lizard that swims and feeds in the sea.» Iguanas are lizards, and this one swims in the sea, so marine means living in or around the sea. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the only lizard that swims and feeds in the sea" still makes sense.
explain: Marine can also be about ships and sailing, or a soldier. Look at the capital letter in «the Marines», and at what the words around it are about. Sea, ships, and soldiers who fight at sea are all clues. When context is not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: Marine means to do with the sea.
fact: «Marine» can also mean to do with ships and sailing.
fact: A marine is a soldier trained to fight both at sea and on land. «He joined the Marines» means he joined that group of soldiers.
fact: «Marine life», «marine biologist» and «marine park» are common phrases.
fact: «The marine iguana is the only lizard that swims and feeds in the sea.»
exercise: «Polar bears are classed as marine mammals.» What does marine mean here? | Made of metal | To do with trains and railways | Very small and light | *To do with the sea and sea life
exercise: What is a marine? | *A soldier trained to fight at sea and on land | A kind of sailing boat | A tiny fish | Sea animal with a shell
exercise: «Sally Lightfoot crabs are bright red crabs that leap from rock to rock.» Find and copy one word that means the sea is nearby. | rock | bright | crabs | *marine
test: A marine biologist studies | the stars in the sky | old castles | *sea life | trains and cars
test: «He joined the Marines.» What does the Marines mean here? | A type of sailing boat | Shops in the high street | Old ships | *A group of soldiers trained to fight at sea and on land
exam: Which sentence uses marine to mean a soldier? | Polar bears are marine mammals. | *He joined the Marines. | Sally Lightfoot crabs are bright red. | The marine iguana swims in the sea.
